    "created_at": "2026-11-22T15:16:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T15:16:32Z",
    "body": "Facts from the second read of PR #3363 (comment 7081172167 on that PR), for the work of this issue. Nothing on `main` calls the new kernel yet (`bin_facets`, `bin_on`); this issue makes the first caller. Before a caller exists on a path that a user can start, these four items are necessary:\n\n1. `crates/gpu/src/shared.rs:22-29` sets no handler for uncaptured errors on the shared device. The default handler of wgpu panics. Install a handler that records the error and makes the call return the CPU result.\n2. `crates/gpu/src/binning_gpu.rs:163-165` waits on the GPU with no time limit. A driver that does not finish and does not report a lost device makes the call hang. Add a time limit with the CPU fallback.\n3. The call blocks. Do not call it from the UI thread (the frame target is 10 ms).\n4. `crates/gpu/src/adapter.rs:78` picks the software adapter first. On a machine with a real GPU, the compute then runs on WARP or llvmpipe. That is against the speed goal of #3336: prefer the hardware adapter for compute, and keep the software adapter for tests.\n\nSmaller: `try_reserve_exact(1)` before each push (`binning.rs:106`, `:251`) makes a cell list grow one element at a time; `try_reserve(1)` is sufficient. No test sets `CAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off` and then calls `bin_facets`, and no test injects a device failure.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
